{"id":"G2004","lemma":"ἐπιτάσσω","transliteration":"epitassō","sayIt":"epitassō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to command","meaning":"ἐπι-τάσσω\n[in LXX for אָמַר, צָוָה, etc. ;]\nto command, charge: with accusative of thing(s), Luk.14:22; with dative of person(s), Mrk.1:27 9:25, Luk.4:36 8:25; id. with accusative of thing(s), Phm 8; id. with inf., Mrk.6:39, Luk.8:31, Act.23:2; id. with imperat., Mrk.9:25; with accusative and inf., Mrk.6:27.†\nSYN.: κελεύω (AS)","glosses":["commands","order","ordered","commanded that","jesus directed","command"],"count":10,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mrk-1","v":27,"renderings":{"bsb":"He commands","kjv":"commandeth"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-6","v":27,"renderings":{"bsb":"commanded that","kjv":"and commanded"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-6","v":39,"renderings":{"bsb":"Jesus directed","kjv":"he commanded"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-9","v":25,"renderings":{"bsb":"command","kjv":"charge"}},{"chapterId":"luk-4","v":36,"renderings":{"bsb":"He commands","kjv":"he commandeth"}},{"chapterId":"luk-8","v":25,"renderings":{"bsb":"He commands","kjv":"he commandeth"}},{"chapterId":"luk-8","v":31,"renderings":{"bsb":"to order","kjv":"he would"}},{"chapterId":"luk-14","v":22,"renderings":{"bsb":"you ordered","kjv":"thou hast commanded"}},{"chapterId":"act-23","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"ordered","kjv":"commanded"}},{"chapterId":"phm-1","v":8,"renderings":{"bsb":"to order","kjv":"to enjoin"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Mark 1:27","note":"They were all amazed, so that they questioned among themselves, saying, “What is this? A new teaching? For with authority he commands even the unclean spirits…","source":"web"},{"ref":"Luke 4:36","note":"Amazement came on all, and they spoke together, one with another, saying, “What is this word? For with authority and power he commands the unclean spirits, and…","source":"web"},{"ref":"Acts 23:2","note":"The high priest, Ananias, commanded those who stood by him to strike him on the mouth.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Philem